From: Escapement
Subject: [PATCH] core0: build the Tamagotchi into the firmware and start it on core 0

The firmware half of the core-0 move. Everything substantial lives in this repo
and is copied in by scripts/sync-firmware.sh; this patch is only the two files
that belong to the firmware tree itself, because a whole-file copy of either
would have to track esp-hosted forever:

  CMakeLists.txt  add the emulator sources to the component
  app_main.c      start tamacore_start() just before the Linux handoff

Why before the handoff and not after: the task waits on its own for the MMU
entry that init_linux_mmap() leaves behind, so starting it early is safe, and
starting it late would race the handoff. It also cannot log -- a high-volume log
hook through the log pipe wedges this board at exactly that moment (ble_hid.c
has the measurement) -- so it publishes progress into the PSRAM window instead
and core 1 reads it from there.

Apply from the esp-hosted tree root, then run ./scripts/sync-firmware.sh from
the Escapement repo before rebuilding.

Measured on hardware 2026-11-10: guest at 4,038,199 emulated cycles/s against a
4,000,000 target, 159 frames in 10 s at 16 fps, worst frame 11 ms late.

diff --git a/esp_hosted_ng/esp/esp_driver/network_adapter/main/CMakeLists.txt b/esp_hosted_ng/esp/esp_driver/network_adapter/main/CMakeLists.txt
index 10d6011..ee81530 100644
--- a/esp_hosted_ng/esp/esp_driver/network_adapter/main/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/esp_hosted_ng/esp/esp_driver/network_adapter/main/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -1,5 +1,7 @@
-set(COMPONENT_SRCS "app_main.c" "slave_bt.c" "cmd.c" "stats.c" "linux_boot.c" "linux_ipc.c" "linux_flash.c" "ble_prov.c" "ble_hid.c" "log_pipe.c" "bond.c" "shmwindow.c")
-set(COMPONENT_ADD_INCLUDEDIRS "./include")
+set(COMPONENT_SRCS "app_main.c" "slave_bt.c" "cmd.c" "stats.c" "linux_boot.c" "linux_ipc.c" "linux_flash.c" "ble_prov.c" "ble_hid.c" "log_pipe.c" "bond.c"
+    # the Tamagotchi runs here now, on core 0 -- see tamacore_task.c
+    "tamacore_task.c" "splb32.c" "ht24lc08.c" "con_v3_ir.c" "splb32_sound.c" "segmap.c")
+set(COMPONENT_ADD_INCLUDEDIRS "./include" ".")
 
 if(CONFIG_IDF_TARGET_ESP32S3)
     list(APPEND COMPONENT_SRCS linux_ll_esp32s3.c)
diff --git a/esp_hosted_ng/esp/esp_driver/network_adapter/main/app_main.c b/esp_hosted_ng/esp/esp_driver/network_adapter/main/app_main.c
index e918164..8664ab1 100644
--- a/esp_hosted_ng/esp/esp_driver/network_adapter/main/app_main.c
+++ b/esp_hosted_ng/esp/esp_driver/network_adapter/main/app_main.c
@@ -731,12 +731,13 @@ void app_main()
 	periph_module_enable(PERIPH_RSA_MODULE);
 
 	/*
-	 * Core 0's writer into the PSRAM megabyte Linux does not own. Started
-	 * before the handoff and silent by design: it publishes into the window
-	 * rather than the log pipe, which wedges the board at this stage.
+	 * The Tamagotchi, on core 0. Started before the handoff and silent by
+	 * design: it publishes into the PSRAM window rather than the log pipe,
+	 * which wedges the board at this stage. It waits for core 1 to put the
+	 * ROM in the window, so this only creates the task.
 	 */
-	void shmwindow_start(void);
-	shmwindow_start();
+	void tamacore_start(void);
+	tamacore_start();
 
 	void linux_boot(void);
 	linux_boot();
